<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shi'a Islam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shi'a</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shi'a Islam is the branch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> that recognises <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a> and his descendants as the rightful leaders of the Muslim community. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> drew on support from pro-Alid groups in its revolution against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s attempt to reconcile Shi'a Islam with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> practice failed to gain acceptance from the clergy.</p></div>
